# DrafterBuckets-1 (2026-10-30): TF_GLM_DRAFT_WIDE=<rows> (default 0: off, the old launches): one stream's DFlash2 context
# update of more than t_max rows (a prompt chunk) runs in eager launches of up to <rows> rows (after the rows it overwrites
# itself in the ring), so the 4-bit fc weight is swept once per L2 group of row tiles instead of once per 64 rows.
# Bit-identical ring rows, device ends and context ends (every kernel of an update is row-independent). With
# <rows>:prompt the wide launches run on the prompt chunks' matmul (qmm.prefill_matmul): other draft bits, same replies.
